Subject: [PATCH] crypto: sun8i-ce: log V851S CE state on cipher timeout
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [temporary V851S hardware diagnostics]

Capture the CE task descriptor, both task address registers, the CE version,
and control/status registers when a V851S cipher request times out. This
distinguishes a task that was not accepted by the engine from one that
completed or faulted without delivering an IRQ.

---
 drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
@@ -242,4 +242,15 @@ int sun8i_ce_run_task(struct sun8i_ce_dev *ce, int flow, const char *name)
 	if (ce->chanlist[flow].status == 0) {
-		dev_err(ce->dev, "DMA timeout for %s on flow %d\n", name, flow);
+		dev_err(ce->dev,
+			"DMA timeout for %s on flow %d: TDA=%08x:%08x VER=%08x ISR=%08x ICR=%08x TLR=%08x TSR=%08x ESR=%08x\n",
+			name, flow, readl(ce->base + CE_TDQ),
+			readl(ce->base + CE_CTR), readl(ce->base + 0x90),
+			readl(ce->base + CE_ISR), readl(ce->base + CE_ICR),
+			readl(ce->base + CE_TLR), readl(ce->base + CE_TSR),
+			readl(ce->base + CE_ESR));
+		if (sun8i_ce_is_v23(ce))
+			print_hex_dump(KERN_ERR, "CE23 TASK: ", DUMP_PREFIX_OFFSET,
+				       16, 4, ce->chanlist[flow].tl, 220, false);
+		else
+			sun8i_ce_dump_task_descriptors(&ce->chanlist[flow]);
 		err = -EFAULT;
 	}
